Entrance Hall
   This is where visitors enter the castle proper, through the wide doorway to 
the north. The doorway is currently blocked by a sturdy portcullis. Oddly, 
there is a doorbell on the inside of the doorway. Other doorways lead east, 
west, and south.
   A proclamation hangs on the wall.

Banquet Hall
Many royal feasts have been held in this hall, which could easily hold ten 
thousand guests. Legends say that Dimwit's more excessive banquets would 
require the combined farm outputs of three provinces. The primary exits are to 
the west and south; smaller openings lead east and northeast.
   You can see a cauldron here.

