royal orchestra, but the musicians (like everyone else) have fled the 
eastlands. Uncountable rows of velvet-covered seats extend into the shadows 
beyond your light. Gilt-trimmed balconies hang above the huge wooden stage. 
A lone spotlight illuminates the conductor's stand. Passages lead east, 
north and south.

