Outer Bailey
   A mighty, rotting tree stump spreads its roots across the bailey.
   The jester appears.
   "While cleaning my attic, I found some old haddock, a hammer and nails, 
some barrels and pails, an old garden gate, and this silly old slate!" He 
hands you the slate. The jester gives a cheerful wave of farewell and 
vanishes, saying, "So long, and thanks for all the fish!" Odd. You've never
given the jester any fish.

