West Shore
What's a castle without a lake? Dimwit loved lakes, but hated to go outside, so
he had one constructed in his extensive cellars. Once a lovely lake, teeming 
with life, its waters have grown stagnant. The scummy surface stretches off to 
the east, and a tunnel leads west.
