     649
>push boulder
You give the boulder a shove. It lurches and begins careening down the 
mountain. Picking up speed, it flattens several trees, hits an outcropping, and
shoots into the air, toward the lake. It lands in the lake with a tremendous 
splash, just missing the blue dock! The rock disappears beneath the water, 
leaving only a series of widening ripples. As you recuperate from the 
excitement, you notice a feature that was formerly blocked by the boulder: a 
small cave leading north into the mountain.
