Ruined Hall
The entrance hall of the summer castle retains but a shadow of its former 
elegance; the ceiling has partially collapsed, and myriad weeds grow amongst 
the debris that covers the floor. A fireplace is choked with the rubble of its 
collapsed chimney. Above the fireplace is a faded fresco, and next to that, a 
tiny vase is mounted on the wall. Arched openings lead north, south and west. A
stairway once led upwards, but there's little left of it.
   The rooster hungrily eyes the worm.

